 running."]}, "overview": "Senator Ed Markey seeks another term in a state that leans 14 points Democratic, and all ten independent ratings place the race as Safe or Solid Democratic. Polling throughout 2026 has been consistent: the latest September surveys showed Markey ahead 52-26 and 53-30, and published averages put his lead around 24 points. Prediction markets price a Markey win at roughly 98 percent.\n\nMarkey also holds a clear financial edge, raising about $5.4 million to Republican John Deaton's $1.6 million, with no outside spending targeting him. Deaton, an attorney and first-time statewide candidate, has drawn notice for combative debate performances, but analysts note the state's arithmetic works against him, particularly given President Trump's standing in Massachusetts. An independent and a minor-party candidate are on the ballot but register minimal support. The realistic question is whether Markey's margin approaches 20 points or exceeds it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9975, "margin": 19.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9987, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9989, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9987, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin